{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-103", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-23-02-ananias-high-priest", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus, Ant. 20.103: Herod of Chalcis 'made Ananias, the son of Nebedeu' high priest in Cumanus's time (c. 47/48 CE) - grade A for the office alone. The office claim ac-23-02-ananias-office (the titles/offices split) and ac-24-01-ananias-high-priest (Acts 24:1) merged into this oldest id."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-137-144", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-23-26-felix-governor", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus, Ant. 20.137: the emperor sent Felix, brother of Pallas, 'as procurator of Judaea' - grade A for Felix's governorship alone (split from claim:ac-23-24-30-letter per the architect's titles/offices ruling)."}
{"from": "passage:ac-23-26", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:ac-23-26-felix-governor", "note": "Acts 23:26 addresses 'the most excellent governor Felix'; the letter event is claim:ac-23-24-30-letter."}
